codex
The implementation audit is complete: generation is genuinely inverse (answer classes are sampled before compatible shifts), the checker does not read `inst["answer"]`, random candidates are uniform over the promised balanced language, and the canonical key was exercised under query reordering and primitive-root coordinate changes. I’m doing the final local run now and will write its exact measurements into `selftest_report.json`.
