codex
Built a native finite-field `TRACK = "B"` generator based on Section 2, Lemma 3.1, and Theorem 3.2 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.04611).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/gen_1505_04611.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1505.04611/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Shipping measurements include:

- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability `1/601080390`
- Four attacks: each 0/8
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, 9,805,696 operations
- Answer: 343 characters, 64 atoms
- Intended route: 260 operations measured, 288 worst case

External hardening remains incomplete: every OpenRouter request returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`, so there were no scored oracle attempts and no hardness verdict is claimed. The genuine script-produced error transcripts are preserved for audit.
